Rule 1 (out tensor must match input dtype and shape to avoid dtype mismatch)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor must not be bool to avoid "ceil_vml_cpu" not implemented for 'Bool')
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor must not be complex to avoid "ceil is not supported for complex inputs")
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 4 (input tensor dtype must be a real numeric type supported by ceil)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
